Array is the list of the item of similar type or class
eg. 
int[] eng= new int[5];
int[] maths= new int[5];
int[] chemistry= new int[5];

instead of making many number of the variable for each subject use Array to store it.

syntax: type[]ArrayName= new type[size];
eg. int[] marks= new int[5];

new= Keyword used to create an object of the array.
[]= array brackets used to declare the array.

to store the value in the array we use index number starting from 0 to (size-1).
Java arrays are called zero-based arrays because the index of the first element is 0, not 1.
eg. 
marks[0]=85; .. marks of eng
marks[1]=90; .. marks of maths
marks[2]=95; .. marks of chemistry

to get stored item in index number we use the same index number to get the value.
eg. System.out.println(marks[0]); // it will print 85
System.out.println(marks[1]); // it will print 90
System.out.println(marks[2]); // it will print 95